                <pb facs="0321" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg215"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Wright.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-01">August 1,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon instructs Ambassador Wright to inform the Japanese Government that the
                    Government of the United States would regard with lively satisfaction the speedy
                    establishment in Manchuria of custom-houses as the best effective refutation of
                    the criticism and complaint now frequently made and as giving proof of the
                    intention of Japan.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
